-- 0161: the six furūq sets of Ghāfir 40:1–3 completed (near_C).
-- near_C: complete the six AL furūq sets shown for Ghāfir 40:1–3 (made in 0140). Every member that was still a
-- draft ('ai_assisted', staging ids, no gloss) was checked against al-Rāghib, then Maqāyīs / Lisān / al-Ṣiḥāḥ /
-- al-ʿAyn / al-Miṣbāḥ / Tāj, and Lane (English). Read-only research; this file only stages the rows.
--   member      → canonical GLOBAL lemma id; staging ids (ALL:NS:*) get merged_into the Qurʾānic lemma
--   basic_gloss → plain English; contrast_note → what sets it apart in its set
--   member_src  → lexicon line (block id + page) — quotes cut from ar_ling_root_lexicon_block_v
--   evidence    → one verse, needle cut from qr_ayah.text_uthmani (word_index from qr_word_occurrence)
--   set_src     → the set's contrast line rewritten to include the new members
-- Promoted (19): punishment نَكِير، مَثُلَات، وَبَال · sin خِطْء، حُوب، حِنْث، إِجْرَام، لَمَم · bounty مَيْسَرَة، بَسْطَة ·
--   coming down نَزَلَ، تَنَزَّلَ، حَلَّ، هَبَطَ · turning back إِيَاب (آبَ)، بَاءَ، فَاءَ، صَدَرَ، اِرْتَدَّ.
-- Split displays: «خَطَأ-خِطأ» → خِطْء (17:31, the sin; خَطَأ of 4:92 is a slip, al-Rāghib p.287);
--   «حَلَّ(أَحَلَّ)» → حَلَّ Form I (أَحَلَّ = to settle someone / make lawful); «صَدَرَ-أَصْدَرَ» → صَدَرَ (99:6; Form IV
--   يُصْدِرَ at 28:23 is "bring the flocks back"); «رَدَّ-اِرْتَدَّ» → اِرْتَدَّ (to turn back; رَدَّ = to send back);
--   «آبَ» → إِيَاب (88:25; the verb آبَ itself is not in the Qurʾān; its staging root was wrongly ابو).
-- Not promoted (no book makes them near-synonyms of نَزَلَ): وَضَعَ = put down, contr. of رَفَعَ (Lisān p.4244, Lane p.3055);
--   خَلَعَ = take off, syn. نَزَعَ (Lisān p.3924, Lane p.787, al-Rāghib p.293). Left as drafts; خَلَعَ's staging id resolved.
-- Fix: «أَصْفَحَ» display → صَفَحَ (0140 already moved the lemma to Form I).
-- al-Raghib has no entry in the corpus for وبل / بوأ / وضع; al-ʿAskarī's al-Furūq is not in the corpus.
